 "description": "Computation only: conditional product / setup / add-on candidates from typed constraints (category, brand, formats, OS, license, budget), optional free text and user-claimed ownership, bound to one published snapshot. Each candidate has fit reasons, a cost breakdown over the offers this channel may disclose, budget fit, acquisition steps, canonical_page and site_entry_page. For a product candidate, canonical_page is the product page on this site; it carries the complete price table (including listings withheld on this channel), the merchant purchase links and the affiliate disclosure. site_entry_page is the same page with the entry marker for this channel. For a setup candidate canonical_page is the /find/ page. No purchase, no persistence, no notification. For a subscription or rent-to-own edition, cost_breakdown.payable_now is the first charge, recurring_cost one later charge (estimated) and recurring_period its period (month or year); with budget_scope=total_including_recurring_12m the total counts 12 monthly or 1 yearly charge, otherwise budget_fit is judged on the first payment. Where a product has one-off and recurring editions, the default scope prices the one-off edition and the 12-month scope the edition with the smallest 12-month total (assumptions key edition_choice). A price is taken from the default confirmed-route class first (a maker store or a confirmed authorized dealer selling new; for hardware also domestic distribution); when a cheaper confirmed listing of the same edition lies outside that class, the candidate's mismatches state it with its amount. search_complete=false with optimality_scope=best_found marks an answer cut at a limit, a free-text term that looks like a product name (Latin letters, digits or katakana) but matches no registered alias (unresolved_constraints no_alias_match), or no candidates (no_candidates). Free-text aliases match whole words only. With a budget, candidates are ordered by budget_fit first (confirmed, estimated_within, estimated_over, over, unknown) before the answer is cut to max_candidates; when in-budget candidates are still cut, limits_hit contains budget_fit_candidates_truncated. An edition with no price in the requested currency keeps its price in the original currency, unconverted, in cost_breakdown and acquisition_steps[].cost, with budget_fit unknown and the reason in the candidate's mismatches. Stale offers (past fresh_until) are not used for costs or budget fit. Bounded compute class (10 per minute, shared with POST /api/v1/resolve). Links are user_navigation handoffs (handoff_mode=user_navigation) and are not intended for prefetching or automatic clicking.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
